From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: voidforge <voidforge@valuz.io>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:59:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: extension keyboard commands and error
 counts

Plan C26.

- Each profile's OACExtensions owns an ExtensionKeybindingRegistry subclass
  (openarc/bridge/oac_extension_commands.mm) that keeps the active
  accelerators of its extensions' `commands` (named commands and
  `_execute_action`, as Chrome's Android registry does). A tab's
  PreHandleKeyboardEvent offers each key press to its profile's registry
  before the page sees it, as Chrome's FocusManager registers extension
  accelerators at high priority: a named command sends commands.onCommand
  with that tab (activeTab granted when asked for); `_execute_action` runs
  the action on the tab, and a popup it opens goes to the delegate
  (-extensions:didOpenPopup:fromKeyboardOnTab:; closed when unhandled).
  Shortcuts keep being edited in chrome://extensions/shortcuts.
- Runtime errors: Chromium's error console already collects them while
  developer mode is on and chrome://extensions lists them; the bridge now
  reports OACExtensionInfo.errorCount and
  -extensions:didChangeErrorsOfExtension: from the console's observer.
